'''Lark and Jonk''', nicknamed '''the twins''', was a [[Danzikan]] who lived during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref>

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Lark and Jonk was created for the [[2018]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Star Wars'' Anthology]] film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''<ref name="Solo" /> and was first revealed in the film's first trailer.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|jPEYpryMp2s|Solo: A Star Wars Story Official Trailer|sw_url=video/official-trailer-solo-a-star-wars-story}}</ref> The character first received identification in the reference book ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]] and released in conjunction with the film.<ref name="TOG" />

In an interview with [[StarWars.com]], creature concept designer [[Jake Lunt Davies]] revealed that for Lark and Jonk' design, like [[Glaucus]]'s, Ivan Manzella was influenced by the space monster feel of the [[1950s]], taking as inspiration what would have influenced the designers had ''Solo'' been released in [[1960s#1965|1965]], twelve years prior to [[1977]], year in which the original ''[[Star Wars]]'' film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], was released.<ref name="Lark and Jonk's Design">{{SW|url=news/solo-a-star-wars-story-designs|text=Inside the Designs of ''Solo: A Star Wars Story''}}</ref>

